1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,390
Japan - Germany

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,150
Japan - Germany

3
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:09,780
The final match of the first National Youth Tournament has finally begun.

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:12,390
Japan, aware of the opponent's habits thanks to Wakabayashi...

5
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:15,850
...dominated the game from the very start.

6
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,970
And they boldly tried their chances.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,230
And they boldly tried their chances.

8
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:25,570
However, the phantom goalkeeper Dieter Müller kept his goal shut tight.

9
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,980
And...

10
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:30,570
Oh, Kaltz makes a misplaced strike.

11
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:32,460
The ball goes in the wrong direction.

12
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:33,610
No, it's not.

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,240
He wanted us to think that, and then sent a perfectly accurate pass.

14
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:39,750
This Hermann Kaltz is cunning.

15
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:42,540
Good.

16
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,080
What!?

17
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:46,840
No, that wasn't a misplaced strike.

18
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:51,230
Germany's other forward, Margas, runs toward where the pass is heading.

19
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:52,610
We scored this time.

20
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:53,860
Damn.

21
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,110
Catch!

22
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,990
Wakabayashi!

23
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:00,370
Wakabayashi!

24
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:02,120
Wakabayashi!

25
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:47,900
Wakabayashi caught it!

26
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:50,520
What!?

27
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,700
One more brilliant save!

28
00:02:58,030 --> 00:02:59,780
Your work was perfect, Wakabayashi.

29
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,380
As I said before the match, except for Schneider...

30
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:07,290
...you can let the others take their shots, easy to save like this.

31
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,540
Wakabayashi!

32
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:12,260
Genzo Wakabayashi.

33
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:17,300
Coach never let me join a club or play a match.

34
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,890
I'm truly resentful of you.

35
00:03:20,350 --> 00:03:24,440
Someone my age was always referred to as Germany's best goalkeeper.

36
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:28,570
But I will clarify this in this match.

37
00:03:28,650 --> 00:03:31,810
Germany's number 1, the world's number 1...

38
00:03:31,810 --> 00:03:35,660
...is only me, Dieter Müller.

39
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:42,290
The German youth return to their positions.

40
00:03:42,370 --> 00:03:45,290
Wakabayashi may have stopped it...

41
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:49,700
...but they displayed their usual attacking play for the first time in this match.

42
00:03:50,050 --> 00:03:54,460
Germany attacks well when they dominate the midfield as they do now.

43
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:57,960
Midfield control seems to be the key to this match.

44
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,100
It seems they've noticed.

45
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:05,060
They've noticed that we know their habits and weak points.

46
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,060
Yes.

47
00:04:06,150 --> 00:04:09,350
Now the real battle begins.

48
00:04:09,610 --> 00:04:11,150
No more tricks!

49
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:13,650
It's time to show real skill.

50
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:16,200
Whatever happens, never lose your fighting spirit!

51
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,610
Okay!

52
00:04:17,610 --> 00:04:21,610
Well, the fierce battle between Japan and Germany continues.

53
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:24,740
Wakabayashi starts the play.

54
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:31,050
And Germany comfortably takes the ball back.

55
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:36,050
The struggle in midfield has intensified.

56
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:39,470
Come on, come on Japan!

57
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,750
Keep going!

58
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,520
Show your fighting spirit!

59
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,760
Good luck!

60
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:47,690
15 minutes of the first half have passed.

61
00:04:47,770 --> 00:04:51,770
Which team will control the midfield and score the first goal?

62
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,570
I'm very excited.

63
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:57,770
This will be the most tense top-level match I've ever played.

64
00:05:00,910 --> 00:05:03,490
They give the ball to Schester.

65
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:05,990
Come on! Great, Schester!

66
00:05:06,710 --> 00:05:07,880
Let's go, Kaltz!

67
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:08,990
Okay.

68
00:05:08,990 --> 00:05:10,500
Let's go, Misaki.

69
00:05:10,590 --> 00:05:11,990
Okay, Tsubasa.

70
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:17,000
The technical Schester and the cunning Kaltz are on the attack.

71
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:21,750
Japan's golden duo, Tsubasa and Misaki, confront them.

72
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,770
Pass it in front of the goal to me.

73
00:05:23,850 --> 00:05:25,230
This time I will score.

74
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,340
For my father and everyone watching, I...

75
00:05:28,190 --> 00:05:30,270
...will score Germany's first goal!

76
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:32,690
Pass to me, Tsubasa.

77
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:35,430
I want to get close to him...

78
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:38,450
...and strike from close range with my new Tiger Shot.

79
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,830
- Now!
- What?

80
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:44,280
Misaki's tackle succeeded.

81
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:46,790
Tsubasa wins the ball.

82
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:48,280
Great, Misaki.

83
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:49,670
You can't pass.

84
00:05:56,010 --> 00:05:57,220
He's getting past!

85
00:05:57,300 --> 00:06:01,630
Tsubasa passes the midfielder Schester with a powerful move.

86
00:06:01,850 --> 00:06:03,060
Good, I got past.

87
00:06:03,130 --> 00:06:05,130
- Well done, Tsubasa!
- Go!

88
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:14,150
Oh, that was a hard tackle.

89
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:17,310
